{"status":"ready","content":"I need to divide 10^30 by 97 and find both the quotient and remainder.\n\nFirst, let me calculate 10^30 ÷ 97.\n\nTo find the quotient and remainder, I'll use the division algorithm: 10^30 = 97q + r, where 0 ≤ r < 97.\n\nLet me calculate 10^30 mod 97 first to find the remainder.\n\nUsing Fermat's Little Theorem: Since 97 is prime and gcd(10, 97) = 1, we have:\n10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nSo I need to find 10^30 mod 97.\n\nLet me calculate powers of 10 mod 97:\n- 10^1 ≡ 10 (mod 97)\n- 10^2 ≡ 100 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^3 ≡ 30 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 300 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^5 ≡ 90 (mod 97)\n- 10^6 ≡ 900 ≡ 27 (mod 97)\n\nLet me use repeated squaring:\n- 10^2 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^8 ≡ 81 (mod 97)\n- 10^16 ≡ 81^2 ≡ 6561 ≡ 6561 - 67(97) ≡ 6561 - 6499 ≡ 62 (mod 97)\n\nNow 30 = 16 + 8 + 4 + 2, so:\n10^30 ≡ 10^16 · 10^8 · 10^4 · 10^2 (mod 97)\n10^30 ≡ 62 · 81 · 9 · 3 (mod 97)\n\nLet me calculate step by step:\n- 62 · 81 = 5022 ≡ 5022 - 51(97) ≡ 5022 - 4947 ≡ 75 (mod 97)\n- 75 · 9 = 675 ≡ 675 - 6(97) ≡ 675 - 582 ≡ 93 (mod 97)\n- 93 · 3 = 279 ≡ 279 - 2(97) ≡ 279 - 194 ≡ 85 (mod 97)\n\nSo the remainder is **85**.\n\nThe quotient is:\nq = (10^30 - 85)/97\n\nq = 10309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567010309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567\n\n**Quotient:** 10309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567\n\n**Remainder:** 85\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Sonnet 4.5","modelId":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5","promptId":"power-division","content":"I need to divide 10^30 by 97 and find both the quotient and remainder.\n\nFirst, let me calculate 10^30 ÷ 97.\n\nTo find the quotient and remainder, I'll use the division algorithm: 10^30 = 97q + r, where 0 ≤ r < 97.\n\nLet me calculate 10^30 mod 97 first to find the remainder.\n\nUsing Fermat's Little Theorem: Since 97 is prime and gcd(10, 97) = 1, we have:\n10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nSo I need to find 10^30 mod 97.\n\nLet me calculate powers of 10 mod 97:\n- 10^1 ≡ 10 (mod 97)\n- 10^2 ≡ 100 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^3 ≡ 30 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 300 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^5 ≡ 90 (mod 97)\n- 10^6 ≡ 900 ≡ 27 (mod 97)\n\nLet me use repeated squaring:\n- 10^2 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^8 ≡ 81 (mod 97)\n- 10^16 ≡ 81^2 ≡ 6561 ≡ 6561 - 67(97) ≡ 6561 - 6499 ≡ 62 (mod 97)\n\nNow 30 = 16 + 8 + 4 + 2, so:\n10^30 ≡ 10^16 · 10^8 · 10^4 · 10^2 (mod 97)\n10^30 ≡ 62 · 81 · 9 · 3 (mod 97)\n\nLet me calculate step by step:\n- 62 · 81 = 5022 ≡ 5022 - 51(97) ≡ 5022 - 4947 ≡ 75 (mod 97)\n- 75 · 9 = 675 ≡ 675 - 6(97) ≡ 675 - 582 ≡ 93 (mod 97)\n- 93 · 3 = 279 ≡ 279 - 2(97) ≡ 279 - 194 ≡ 85 (mod 97)\n\nSo the remainder is **85**.\n\nThe quotient is:\nq = (10^30 - 85)/97\n\nq = 10309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567010309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567\n\n**Quotient:** 10309278350515463917525773195876288659793814432989690721649484536082474226804123711340206185567\n\n**Remainder:** 85\n","inferredMetadata":{"inferred":true,"sourcePath":"scripts/responses/claude-sonnet-4-5/power-division.txt","modelSlug":"claude-sonnet-4-5","modelFamily":"claude_mid_tier","modelReleaseDate":"Sep 2025","modelSource":"openrouter"},"prompt":{"id":"power-division","text":"Divide 10^30 by 97 and give the quotient and remainder.","tags":["reasoning","math"]}},"path":"responses/claude-sonnet-4-5/power-division.json","size":2160,"mtime":1779392170}